# A route tree: a square trunk under two canopy cones.
# Y is up, +Z is the way the creature faces, one world unit is one map tile.
# The lowest vertex sits on y = 0 and the model is centred on x = 0 and z = 0,
# so the game places it by its feet.
#
# Faces are wound so that (c - a) x (b - a) points out of the solid, which is
# what tools/obj2cpp.py bakes as the face normal. Get it backwards and the
# model still draws, it just goes flat ambient dark.
#
# Eyes are not modelled. They are two depth tested dots in the 2D layer, which
# is a pixel each instead of eight triangles.
#
# About 2.50 units tall, 20 triangles. tree_far.obj is the same
# silhouette for six, and a tree that swaps between them must not
# visibly change shape, which is why both canopies are six sided.

mtllib tree.mtl

# trunk, 8 triangles
v 0.105 0.900 0.105
v -0.105 0.900 0.105
v -0.105 0.900 -0.105
v 0.105 0.900 -0.105
v 0.130 0.000 0.130
v -0.130 0.000 0.130
v -0.130 0.000 -0.130
v 0.130 0.000 -0.130
usemtl tree_trunk
f 1 5 6 2
f 2 6 7 3
f 3 7 8 4
f 4 8 5 1

# lower canopy, 6 triangles
v 0.000 1.770 0.000
v 0.860 0.720 0.000
v 0.430 0.720 0.745
v -0.430 0.720 0.745
v -0.860 0.720 0.000
v -0.430 0.720 -0.745
v 0.430 0.720 -0.745
usemtl tree_leaf_low
f 9 10 11
f 9 11 12
f 9 12 13
f 9 13 14
f 9 14 15
f 9 15 10

# upper canopy, 6 triangles
v 0.000 2.500 0.000
v 0.620 1.450 0.000
v 0.310 1.450 0.537
v -0.310 1.450 0.537
v -0.620 1.450 0.000
v -0.310 1.450 -0.537
v 0.310 1.450 -0.537
usemtl tree_leaf_high
f 16 17 18
f 16 18 19
f 16 19 20
f 16 20 21
f 16 21 22
f 16 22 17
